# SitePro Next.js Application

This rule applies to work inside `frontend/web/`.

Before implementing or modifying frontend functionality, read:

`frontend/web/AGENTS.md`

Also consult relevant documents under:

- `docs/product/`
- `docs/architecture/`

## Product UX

The primary website-management experience is website-first.

Do not turn normal website editing into a traditional CMS dashboard
with persistent heavy sidebars or configuration screens.

Prefer:

AI assistance
→ direct website editing
→ advanced controls when necessary.

The website should remain visually dominant during editing.

## Backend Integration

Laravel is the authoritative API/domain layer.

Do not reproduce backend authorization or authoritative business rules
as frontend-only logic.

Frontend validation may improve UX, but security-sensitive validation
must also exist in the API.

## Design References

Use `docs/designs/` as visual reference when available.

Design mockups may contain illustrative content.

Do not assume that pricing, AI allowances, example domains, account
information, plan limits, or other sample values shown in mockups are
actual requirements.

Follow the product specification when a mockup and documented behavior
differ.